# V1b (STOP). IMAGE: tp4-stackfix-3 (built by V0b). V1a on the pairs profile (QWEN_FAST_QUAD_DRAFT=0, singles audit all): the pair at four
# cards, every pair round audited against the members' own single-user drafts. PASS as V1a, with pair rounds in place of the quad.
# CHECKS (c2_smoke_check, four cards): the "four-card eager prefill warmed before the packed traces" line exists and PRECEDES Metal's
# "Allocating device buffers is unsafe due to the existence of an active trace" warning, and no "[PINDIAG] four-card prefill programs=A->B
# window=W" line has B-A-W above zero (a program compiled after the capture: #48536, the hang this job hit on tp4-stackfix-2).
# Duration (estimate): 11-14 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over the job file on a throwaway
# commit of tp4/stack-fix (or a descendant) and push the window tag. Nothing here names a rig, a card or a registry. The smoke and its
# check run from the CHECKOUT on the rig host; the server is the IMAGE'S baked tree (--read-only, no bind mount), so C2_IMAGE_TAG picks
# the server and the checkout picks the smoke and the check. THE DRIVER SUBSTITUTES C2_IMAGE_TAG FROM ITS IMAGE_TAG ENV: a chain that
# sets one IMAGE_TAG for all its jobs runs every job on that image, so jobs that need different images are SEPARATE ONE-JOB CHAINS.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-stackfix-3
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate-pairs
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady
